  "claim": "Australian magazines, \"Woman's Day\", \"New Idea\" and one other, were edited by Nene Claire King. That other magazine and the magazine The Prince and Betty was published in are both monthly magazines.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Ainslee's Magazine. Sentence: Ainslee's Magazine was an American literary periodical published from 1897 to December 1926.\nPage: The Australian Women's Weekly. Sentence: The Australian Women's Weekly, sometimes known as simply \"The Weekly\", is an Australian monthly women's magazine published by Bauer Media Group in Sydney.\nPage: The Prince and Betty. Sentence: It was originally published in \"Ainslee's Magazine\" in the United States in January 1912, and, in a slightly different form, as a serial in \"Strand Magazine\" in the United Kingdom between February and April 1912.\nPage: Nene King. Sentence: She is the former editor of some of Australia's most famous women's magazines, including \"Woman's Day\", \"New Idea\" and \"Women's Weekly\".",
